// name :
"P313710717" "Eye of Judgement (Dark Astoria Prologue)"
// teamrequiresfailedtext :
"P3934466014" "<color orange>You and everyone on your team must be a VIP to run Dark Astoria content.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Fortunata 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3703793585" "Castrin Fleeing"
// DetailString :
"P2596132895" "There was no operative at the platform when you arrived. You looked around and spotted an operative watching you from the slums. He stumbled into one of the buildings after seeing you.<br><br>This must be the operative that's seeking to destroy you!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - AstoriaClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P139519325" "Astoria Documents"
// DetailString :
"P3256308406" "You searched an abandoned car and discovered documents that detail what city you're in. It seems you've somehow ended up in Dark Astoria, a part of Paragon City that was abandoned some time ago when a group called the Banished Pantheon took it over.<br><br>You look around and spot a member of the Circle of Thorns nearby. He seems to be cowering in fear at something. Perhaps you can get information out of him regarding <i>what</i> exactly is going on here."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL9_ArachnosThreat 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1253738499" "Image of Dark Tunnels"
// tDetailString :
"P4039250227" "You remember the image of a dark tunnel with a glowing light at the end of it. You somehow ended up in there after going through an old apartment. It reminds you of a small journey called...<br><br><b>Eye of Judgement</b><br><br>It started when an Arachnos operative named Castrin send you a threatening letter, claiming that he would stop at nothing to see you destroyed. You decided to look into Castrin and contacted Arbiter Daos to see where this operative was stationed. What happened next was a chase; Castrin had already fled when you arrived to his station. You chased him into an old building and lost him in one of the apartments. You went to enter a door and somehow ended up in a dark forest. You tried to push through the forest but appeared in an old subway tunnel. You were then flung through a deep hole, ending up within the cursed city of Dark Astoria.<br><br>You can only guess that whatever sent you into Dark Astoria also spurred Operative Castrin to want to kill you. Some great and powerful entity seems to want you dead. They'll have to try a lot harder than that."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Hazen 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1462045980" "<color orange>The man in the forest speaks to you, though he does not look at you.</color><br><br>It begins again. The ebb and flow, back and forth. More march to the slaughter which we all hoped to stop. But we were cast out, called insane, after our work was done.<br><br>No one would try to remember the past, how hard we fought to save the future."
// Answer Text :
"P3890908801" "Where is Operative Castrin?"
// Page Castrin Text :
"P3820664354" "Castrin. I saw the man, he fell into here too. He went mad and was destroyed. He kept muttering a name, over and over again.<br><br>He is like all the others who had been chosen. He could not bear it, the nightmares took him over. It chose something he despised and used it to devour his essence.<br><br>If you were after Castrin, you will only find him in the next life."
// Answer Text :
"P405491381" "Who are you?"
// Answer Text :
"P809685580" "Where am I?"
// Page WhoAreYou Text :
"P1659768877" "No one. I was someone, once, but now, I am no one. I was cast out for what I did, for what we all did. They called us crazy, they couldn't believe what we said.<br><br>We tried to save the world, and we were destroyed for it. Now, the world is paying for the sins of the past, for the sin of forgetting the past."
// Answer Text :
"P2817404675" "What do you mean?"
// Page WhatDoYouMean Text :
"P3525321459" "<color orange>The man remains silent, refusing to answer your question. You notice that he is somewhat ethereal, a ghost.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"
// Page WhereAmI Text :
"P388412094" "The border of life and death. Its world, or rather, part of it. I've been here before, when we first fought.<br><br>If you're here, it means <i>it</i> wants you, just like it wanted me so long ago. There's no turning back now. If it wants you, it will find a way to get you closer and closer. That's what happened with me, but it wasn't expecting what I did, not that it mattered, in the end."
// Answer Text :
"P979349640" "What is this 'it'?"
// Page WhatIsIt Text :
"P198560438" "<color orange>The man remains silent, his hands shaking at a thought. You notice that he is slightly see through, indicating that he must be a ghost.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Heather 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1268988770" "<color orange>The woman before you seems to look worn out, the circles around her eyes indicating that she has either not slept for days, or has barely slept at all. She takes a few steps back as you step past the runes.</color><br><br>Stay back, {HeroName}! I don't know why the runes aren't stopping <i>you</i>... but I'll do what I can to fight you!<br><br>Was this all your doing? Dark Astoria coming back to life? The monsters roaming the streets?"
// Answer Text :
"P350241873" "I wish I could take credit, but it was not my doing."
// Answer Text :
"P202295524" "No, I have nothing to do with this."
// Page NotMe Text :
"P3217540645" "Then what are you here for? There's nothing for you to gain in this cursed place, {HeroName}!"
// Answer Text :
"P1494415687" "I'm here to save the day."
// Answer Text :
"P2821683522" "I'll be playing the role of the hero today."
// Page SavetheDay Text :
"P4106150641" "<i>You</i>? Save the day? Are you kidding me?"
// Answer Text :
"P2509394468" "I need this world together just as much as you do."
// Page PlayingHeroRole Text :
"P2360788367" "And then what about tomorrow? This place is full of sin, {HeroName}, we don't need more of it from you here."
// Answer Text :
"P2116935527" "You need me here to fight this."
// Page NeedThisWorld Text :
"P2703575905" "<color orange>Heather Townshend grumbles.</color><br><br>I suppose you're right. Very well.<br><br>My name is Heather Townshend. This situation must be really bad if it's up to someone like <i>you</i> to fight this, but... well, most <i>villains</i> are usually arrested at this point. Someone as smart and powerful as yourself could be our best shot at fighting this thing. I'll tell you what you need to know."
// Answer Text :
"P2379326880" "What are you doing here? And what are these runes?"
// Page Runes Text :
"P3638131447" "I can't really answer either of those very well, but I'll do my best. A while back, I began to feel a... pull to Dark Astoria. Something was calling me to return. I used to live here, before the city was taken over by these monsters.<br><br>When I entered the city, something felt wrong, more than usual. It felt like something was on the brink of bursting forth. There were these strange winged creatures flying towards the cemetery. Some of them were attacking some women who were armed to the teeth, they looked like assassins.<br><br>I hid in the shadows as I watched as these winged women fight these assassins. The monsters called them traitors to the cause. Their fight was interrupted by this... this <i>horrible</i> moaning in the distance, followed by a violent earthquake. Something must have burst out of the cemetery. The monsters killed the assassins and departed. I felt an incredibly force overcome me, and I blacked out."
// Answer Text :
"P827121431" "And then?"
// Page AndThen Text :
"P2315541299" "I woke up where we're standing right now, surrounded by these protective runes. There were two people with me, a man named <color yellow>Kadabra Kill</color> and his wife, <color yellow>Sigil</color>. I asked them where the runes came from, but they said they did not know. All they knew was that they were enough to hold back the darkness and the monsters, but they would not last for long.<br><br>They both told me to leave, that they would help get me out, but I refused. I... came here to finish something, {HeroName}, something that had been bothering me for a long time, and I intend to do just that. They asked that if I saw anyone else that I ask them to help their investigation.<br><br>They said they were part of some secret organization that was seeking to find out what was happening in Dark Astoria and put a stop to it. I guess that you would count as someone who could help their investigation, right? They did say <i>anyone</i>, after all."
// Answer Text :
"P3518174214" "I'll do what I can to stop this."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Daos 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1528842303" "{HeroName}. You wish to know the location of Operative Castrin?<br><br>He is one of our newer operatives. Why would you wish to know his location?"
// Answer Text :
"P3529935209" "He threatened to kill me."
// Answer Text :
"P3223247093" "He may be a Longbow spy."
// Answer Text :
"P2039625337" "Just tell me what I need to know, Daos."
// Page KillMe Text :
"P3874100910" "Hrm, most disturbing. I can assure you, {HeroName}, that this was not approved by Arachnos. Firstly, we would not be so... direct. Secondly, we are quite aware of your new level of power.<br><br>We are busy enough here trying to deal with the apparent situation in Dark Astoria. <color orange>We've got enough problems dealing with this 'Midnighter Club' and the portal they've set up in Grandville to enter that city.</color> I shall give you the honor of dealing with Castrin.<br><br>He should be near one of the platforms overlooking the slums. If he survives the ordeal with you, then he shall be promoted right away. If he is destroyed, then it will send a message to others in Arachnos not to work outside of our protocols."
// Answer Text :
"P70252942" "Excellent."
// Answer Text :
"P4127636224" "What is the situation in Dark Astoria?"
// Page DarkAstoria Text :
"P2579143856" "If you must know, we have received word that some sort of massive power just spiked in the area. Whatever was sleeping beneath that city is now <i>very</i> awake.<br><br>We are preparing a team to go and investigate what exactly is happening there."
// Answer Text :
"P2642806219" "I understand. I'll be off to deal with Operative Castrin."
// Page LongbowSpy Text :
"P3566366055" "He is not a Longbow spy, {HeroName}. We've had enough of those in the past that we are quite strict in examining our operatives.<br><br>What is it that you want with Operative Castrin?"
// Answer Text :
"P3369600863" "Look, just tell me what I need to know, Daos."
// Page TellMe Text :
"P2157536168" "And why should I tell you his location, {HeroName}?"
// Answer Text :
"P2774092343" "I do believe Recluse made me an honorary Arbiter for defeating Reichsman."
// Answer Text :
"P1333966588" "I took down the Freedom Phalanx, Daos. I think that earns me information."
// Answer Text :
"P1424778781" "I'm an Incarnate, Daos. Do you want to say no to me?"
// Page Reichsman Text :
"P3040340996" ""Hrmmph... I had nearly forgotten about that. Very well, {HeroName}, I'll give you the information. I don't have time to argue, not with the situation in Dark Astoria. <color orange>We've got enough problems dealing with this 'Midnighter Club' and the portal they've set up in Grandville to enter that city.</color><br><br>Castrin should be near one of the platforms overlooking the slums. If he survives the ordeal with you, then he shall be promoted right away. If he is destroyed, then it will send a message to others in Arachnos not to work outside of our protocols."
// Page Phalanx Text :
"P956012938" ""And Arachnos is still thankful for your work against the Phalanx. <br><br>...Very well, {HeroName}, I'll give you the information. I don't have time to argue, not with the situation in Dark Astoria. <color orange>We've got enough problems dealing with this 'Midnighter Club' and the portal they've set up in Grandville to enter that city.</color><br><br>Castrin should be near one of the platforms overlooking the slums. If he survives the ordeal with you, then he shall be promoted right away. If he is destroyed, then it will send a message to others in Arachnos not to work outside of our protocols."
// Page Incarnate Text :
"P1148600849" ""...Very well, {HeroName}, I'll give you the information. I don't have time to argue, not with the situation in Dark Astoria, and I wouldn't wish to cause a scene here with someone at your power. <color orange>We've got enough problems dealing with this 'Midnighter Club' and the portal they've set up in Grandville to enter that city.</color><br><br>Castrin should be near one of the platforms overlooking the slums. If he survives the ordeal with you, then he shall be promoted right away. If he is destroyed, then it will send a message to others in Arachnos not to work outside of our protocols."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - CoT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1974075654" "<color orange>This member of the Circle of Thorns seems to be terrified, either of you or someone else. He stutters when you approach him.</color><br><br>It's... it's {HeroName}! Stay back! The others are gone, inside of it now, but I won't be taken!"
// Answer Text :
"P3289301431" "Calm down, I'm just here for information."
// Answer Text :
"P3108337251" "(Rough up the mage)"
// Page Information Text :
"P1360194117" "You don't understand, there's no <i>calming</i> here! The beast has awakened, the end of the world is upon us!<br><br>No one is safe, not the Circle, not <i>you</i>, no one!"
// Answer Text :
"P1450701795" "What are you talking about?"
// Page TalkingAbout Text :
"P3005988382" "We failed, that is all I know. Some were trying to stop this, but they failed, and now, it has spilled over!<br><br>The power here... it can consume us all! There's nothing like it in this world...!"
// Answer Text :
"P2332395968" "Can this power be harnessed somehow?"
// Answer Text :
"P3114310761" "How can this power be stopped?"
// Page HarnessPower Text :
"P2412910422" "I... I suppose any power can be used, if you knew how to bind it. But it would take an incredible amount to just <i>do</i> it! Whatever is awakened is too powerful now, you'd need to weaken it, somehow, but I wouldn't even know how to begin to do that!"
// Answer Text :
"P3039642464" "There has to be someone here trying to stop this."
// Page StopPower Text :
"P1113980436" "There is another mage nearby, named <color yellow>Maharaj</color>. I think he's here to stop this, but it's hopeless! He'll never stop the lumbering beast! Even if you wanted to take its power for yourself, you would have to weaken it, which is impossible!<br><br><color orange>If what this mage is saying is true, then the power of whatever has awakened can be harnessed if it's weakened. You'll just need to acquire an item to actually <i>use</i> its power, which is something you can look for along the way. In the meantime, you'll have to see what you can do about getting the creature in a state where you can take its power.<br><br>It shouldn't be too difficult to accomplish; after all, when it comes to world-shattering events around here, people seem to be incredibly willing to work together with villains for the 'greater good'. You'll just go along until the time is right and then make your move!"
// Answer Text :
"P1371024413" "I'll find Maharaj, then."
// Page RoughUp Text :
"P2491493082" "<color orange>You use your abilities to rough up the Circle mage. He staggers backwards, pleading.</color><br><br>Please, no more, I'll tell you whatever it is you want to know!"
// Answer Text :
"P1762649765" "I want to know what's going on here."
// Page WhatsGoingOn Text :
"P3788603785" "Something dark has awakened, something that the Circle has been trying to keep contained for a long time.<br><br>I was not privy into what exactly it was; all I know is that we <i>failed</i> to keep it sealed several years ago, and we've failed to keep it from growing out of control.<br><br>It's the end of the world as we know it, {HeroName}. This is not some threat that can be stopped, not even by an Incarnate like yourself!"
// Answer Text :
"P3904563150" "There must be someone out here trying to stop this."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P414074170" "<color orange>You read through the letter...<br><br>{HeroName}!<br><br>You have been running through my dreams. I see you and the horrors you've committed. Arachnos has sat by and allowed this to happen. Heroes have tried to stop you, but to no avail. In all my dreams, you end up killing me. I see you appearing out of the corner of my eye during the day, as if you are stalking me.<br><br>No more! I know the monsters that you are part of. They are worse than anything Arachnos has. I will destroy you, {HeroName}, and this letter of mine intends to show just how serious I am. I do not care how powerful you are, I will defy what my dreams predict. Once you're destroyed, I will find peace in my dreams, and no longer will I hear the whispers trying to beckon me back to Dark Astoria.<br><br>Operative Castrin</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P579102021" "Hrm..."
// SendOffString :
"P245666155" "<color orange>This Operative Castrin seems like he's trying to act on his own, outside of Arachnos approval. You could always just ignore him; judging by his letter, he isn't a Bane Spider or a Fortunata, perhaps just one of the lower class operatives of Arachnos. However, even the smallest threat could appear at an inconvenient moment to stop you.<br><br>You decide to find out where this operative is by speaking with Arbiter Daos. He should know the location of most Arachnos operatives. If he has any qualms with what you're doing, then he can see what it's like trying to deal with someone fueled with the power of an Incarnate."
// TaskTitle :
"P2752941157" "<color deepskyblue>Eye of Judgement</color>"

